WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.070 --> 00:00:03.510
In Konya, a reed flute begins to play.

2
00:00:03.560 --> 00:00:06.880
Dervishes in white skirts start to turn.

3
00:00:06.930 --> 00:00:10.520
The poet Rumi opened his
great poem with a reed flute,

4
00:00:10.570 --> 00:00:13.460
crying for the reed-bed it was cut from.

5
00:00:13.510 --> 00:00:16.720
In a quiet room, a Sufi
counts prayer beads,

6
00:00:16.770 --> 00:00:18.950
repeating a name of God.

7
00:00:19.000 --> 00:00:23.770
So why would a Muslim who already prays
five times a day choose a teacher and

8
00:00:23.820 --> 00:00:25.440
a path of training?

9
00:00:25.490 --> 00:00:29.540
In this mission, you'll meet a famous
hadith that describes three levels of the

10
00:00:29.590 --> 00:00:30.590
religion.

11
00:00:30.640 --> 00:00:34.250
Then you'll compare spoken
and silent remembrance of God,

12
00:00:34.300 --> 00:00:36.980
and read Rumi's Song of the Reed.

13
00:00:37.030 --> 00:00:42.090
Your mission: find out why a Muslim who
already prays would choose a teacher and

14
00:00:42.140 --> 00:00:42.840
a path.
